---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { projectContact } from '../lib/contact';
import '../styles/visitor.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="Discuss a project | Contact Fidret" description="Bring a workflow, system or project question to Hadi Abou Daya. Start with what happens today, what needs to change and the people and constraints involved." canonical="https://fidret.com/contact/">
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="visitor-hero shell">
      <h1>Discuss a project</h1>
      <p class="visitor-lead">Tell Hadi what happens today and what you want to change.</p>
      <p>Start with a task, a recurring problem or a question from the work on this site. You can use Hadi’s personal contact page to describe it; you do not need a finished specification.</p>
      <p>If a particular example prompted your question, include its page link.</p>
      <a class="button" href={projectContact.destination}>{projectContact.destinationLabel}</a>
      <p class="contact-destination">{projectContact.note}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="contact-preparation shell" aria-labelledby="context-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="context-title">Useful starting context</h2>
        <p>A short description or one worked example can explain where the difficulty lies.</p>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>The task and how people carry it out today.</li>
        <li>One example of a delay, error or decision you want to improve.</li>
        <li>The information, equipment, access or timing limits involved.</li>
        <li>Who uses the result, who reviews it and who can authorize changes.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="visitor-split shell">
      <h2>Choose a question to examine first</h2>
      <div>
        <p>For example: how long can a reading support a decision? Can two plans use the same water allocation? Does a release check cover the version being deployed?</p>
        <p>A first discussion can identify which part to investigate, what evidence is available and who needs to be involved. Scope, responsibilities and success criteria belong in the brief before a commitment.</p>
        <div class="visitor-actions">
          <a class="text-link" href="/approach/">How we approach a project</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/people/hadi/">About Hadi</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
